
# ${SHADOW_NAME}: how many copies of GET ${SHADOW_PATH} this box sends to the
# read shadow service: ${SHADOW_RATE} a second and none more at once (no
# burst), so one copy in every quarter second at most. The zone is used in the copy's
# location (/_polis_shadow/${SHADOW_NAME}) and nowhere else, so it counts
# copies only: the request Node answers is never counted, delayed or refused
# by it. A copy over the rate ends in that location with 429 before any
# connection is opened, and its shadow_mirror line says so
# ("mirror_status":429 with an empty "mirror_upstream_status"); with nodelay
# no copy waits. The key is the shadow's name, so the zone holds one state
# for the whole box. limit_req_log_level info keeps a refusal out of the
# error log, which is written from notice up and whose lines name the peer
# address.
limit_req_zone $polis_shadow_name zone=polis_shadow_${SHADOW_NAME}:1m rate=${SHADOW_RATE}r/s;
